phase P3
title Operation kernels
tasks
    T300
        title        Implement the canonical store owner
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D1,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.C2,
                     @plan.Operations.V1,
                     @plan.Operations.V2,
                     @plan.Operations.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.1 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-005, PROOF-006, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver one Runtime-scoped StoreKernel with immutable canonical entries,
            monotonic revisions, metadata, retained bases, actor-effective views, and
            final-owner collection. Keep RcMap limited to leases and garbage collection.
            Passive reads must not create ownership or start work.

            Absorb the store, revision, and passive-read proof obligations from retired
            flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed). Source lineage: flow-state-e7p.12.11 and
            flow-state-e7p.13.12 were closed at migration. Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is
            provenance for Workflow blocker @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation.
            Source phase flow-state-e7p.3 depended on flow-state-e7p.12 and
            flow-state-e7p.27 (open) and flow-state-e7p.13 (closed) at migration. The .13
            administrative prerequisite was satisfied historically; these Beads edges are
            provenance, not Workflow blockers or proof. Workflow @task.Rewrite.T271 is the
            current Phase 3 validation blocker.
            Coordinate with the phase integrator.

            Keep the private store owner under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/store/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Treat this as an implementation boundary; keep facade exports in their
            existing routes. Do not edit the frozen package.
        acceptance
            - Same-Runtime actors share canonical bases while keeping overlays and
            lifetimes independent; separate Runtimes remain isolated.
            - Missing reads create no entry, lease, freshness, revision, or work.
            Older snapshots stay immutable and capture sees no half-commit.
            - Invalid identity fails before mutation; defects and interruption retain
            the prior StoreState.
            - Focused store-owner tests pass in the local test/ subtree, and nub run
            lint passes for the changed slice.

    T301
        title        Implement resource generations and finite occurrences
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T300, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D1,
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.C2,
                     @plan.Operations.Q1,
                     @plan.Operations.V1,
                     @plan.Operations.V2,
                     @plan.Operations.V3,
                     @plan.Operations.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.2 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-005, PROOF-006, PROOF-007, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver bounded canonical-key validation, descriptor/key generation
            identity, first-live executable-input pinning, resource ensure/refetch and
            action admission, non-reused actor-incarnation ordinals, and generation
            fencing through the production completion path.

            Absorb resource identity, canonical-bound, generation, and fencing proofs
            from retired flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed). Source lineage:
            flow-state-e7p.12.11 and flow-state-e7p.13.12 were closed at migration.
            Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is provenance for Workflow blocker
            @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation. Verify pinned scheduling
            and cancellation APIs before implementation claims.

            Keep the private resource-generation owner under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns resource generations and
            finite occurrences. This placement adds no public API route. Do not add
            generic registries or edit the frozen package.
        acceptance
            - Equal canonical keys join one generation and retain its live input;
            explicit refetch starts a new generation.
            - Rejected admission consumes no ordinal. Completion settles once, and
            stale generations or actor incarnations cannot publish.
            - Declarations and passive reads start no work. Decisive owner tests cover
            canonical bounds, typed failures, defects, cancellation, and cleanup.
            - Focused resource-owner tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T302
        title        Implement transactions and explicit writes
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T300, @T301, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D1,
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.V3,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Operations.O2]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.3 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-005, PROOF-006, PROOF-007, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver actor-local transaction identity and concurrency policies,
            admitted occurrences, truthful cancellation boundaries, ordered preview
            layers, canonical-base compare-and-swap, rollback with later-layer replay,
            unknown and reconcile-required truth, and explicit setData only.

            Absorb transaction race, cancellation, and failure-truth proofs from
            retired flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed). Source lineage:
            flow-state-e7p.12.11 and flow-state-e7p.13.12 were closed at migration.
            Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is provenance for Workflow blocker
            @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation. Keep the
            private transaction owner under packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/
            and its local test/ subtree. Within this owner directory, this task owns
            transaction admission, previews, and explicit writes. Keep public exports
            on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Equal transaction keys remain actor-local; cancel and replacement use
            distinct occurrences.
            - Failed preview rollback preserves later layers. Post-boundary results
            report uncertainty instead of claiming the write was undone.
            - No result is promoted and no invalidation or clear is implicit.
            Production-owner tests cover policy order and failure cleanup.
            - Focused transaction tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T303
        title        Implement streams and continuing activities
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T300, @T301, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.C2,
                     @plan.Operations.Q1,
                     @plan.Operations.V3,
                     @plan.Operations.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.4 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-006, PROOF-007, PROOF-014 prerequisite, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver declaration-slot identity, state-scoped reconciliation, exact
            retain/release/replace behavior, shared generation leases, and latest-value
            projections. Explicit mappings and writes are the only transition inputs.
            Finalize once and rematerialize from live input without replay.

            Absorb stream projection, finalization, rematerialization, and activity
            ownership proofs from retired flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed). Source lineage:
            flow-state-e7p.12.11 and flow-state-e7p.13.12 were closed at migration.
            Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is provenance for Workflow blocker
            @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation. Keep the
            private stream/activity owner under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns continuing activity and stream
            lifecycle. Keep public exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Equal normalized plans retain their owner; changed identity releases
            once and replaces once. Duplicate live streams reject.
            - Projection-only emissions do not transition. Terminal streams stay
            terminal; rematerialization does not replay prior emissions.
            - Actor cancellation finalizes once, and no public actor-cancel or child
            actor owner is added.
            - Focused stream/activity tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T304
        title        Implement timers and deterministic polling
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T303, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.Q1,
                     @plan.Operations.V3,
                     @plan.Operations.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.5 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-006, PROOF-007, PROOF-009 prerequisite, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver machine-wide typed timer identity, Runtime Clock deadlines,
            compound lifetime and reentry behavior, deterministic equal-deadline
            ordering, generation fencing, and suspension/disposal release. Refresh a
            settled resource explicitly, with at most one exact-key refresh in flight.

            Absorb timer ordering and fencing proofs from retired flow-state-e7p.3.7
            (closed). Source lineage: flow-state-e7p.12.11 and flow-state-e7p.13.12
            were closed at migration. Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is provenance for Workflow
            blocker @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation. Do not rely on scheduler
            start timing for correctness.
            Keep the private timer owner and local tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns timer and polling behavior.
            Keep public exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Timers cannot admit finite work. Clock movement alone does not execute
            Story work.
            - Each due generation is consumed once in deterministic order; suspension
            and disposal fence stale deadlines and release timer ownership.
            - Polling has no public poll API, implicit retry, or stale completion.
            Focused timer tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T305
        title        Implement StoreFanout and trusted writes
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T300, @T301, @T302, @T303, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D1,
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.C2,
                     @plan.Operations.V1,
                     @plan.Operations.V2,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.6 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-003, PROOF-005, PROOF-006, PROOF-007, PROOF-012 prerequisite.

            Deliver causal StoreFanout after committed actor publication, adjacent
            projection coalescing, exact dependency replacement, atomic invalidate and
            clear batches bounded to 256 identities, active-work fencing, missing
            target no-ops, and scoped
            HostWriteLease provenance and revocation.

            Absorb StoreFanout and invalidation handoff proofs from retired
            flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed). Source lineage: flow-state-e7p.12.11 and
            flow-state-e7p.13.12 were closed at migration. Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is
            provenance for Workflow blocker @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates implementation.
            Keep the private fanout owner and local tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/store/ and its local test/ subtree. Within
            that owner directory, this task owns fanout and trusted writes. Keep public
            exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Fanout never calls actors directly or exposes stale or half-published
            truth. Actors reread current Store state after revision facts.
            - A valid batch within the 256-identity limit makes one mutation and
            revision; invalid or over-bound batches make none. Writes fence active
            work without creating occurrences.
            - Stale revisions do not publish; there is no public writer or cache-wide
            clear path. Tests assert observable atomicity and causal ordering.
            - Focused fanout/store tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T306
        title        Validate Phase 3 owners and proof coverage
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T300, @T301, @T302, @T303, @T304, @T305, @task.Rewrite.T271]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Operations.D1,
                     @plan.Operations.D2,
                     @plan.Operations.C1,
                     @plan.Operations.C2,
                     @plan.Operations.Q1,
                     @plan.Operations.V1,
                     @plan.Operations.V2,
                     @plan.Operations.V3,
                     @plan.Operations.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V3
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.3.8 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.3 (open).

            Run the read-only Phase 3 correctness gate over changed slices and their
            named production-owner proofs. Check module layout, task boundaries,
            failure and cleanup lanes, and required retention/deletion evidence.
            Review this phase only; do not re-audit unchanged phases or the full pack.

            The retired proof tracker flow-state-e7p.3.7 (closed) is absorbed by
            T300–T305; its closure did not claim completed proofs. Source lineage:
            flow-state-e7p.13.12 was closed at migration. Bead flow-state-e7p.27.8 is
            provenance for Workflow blocker @task.Rewrite.T271, which gates validation.
            Coordinate with the Rewrite integrator before validation.

            Outcome disposition: T302 owns Operations O2. Operations O1 spans T300,
            T301, T302, T303, and T305; O3 spans T301, T303, and T304; O4 spans
            T301–T304. Those outcomes remain deferred until the integrated owners
            deliver their full behavior and proof coverage.
        acceptance
            - Each operation owner has a decisive production-path behavior proof and
            focused checks pass. nub run lint passes for the changed slices.
            - Check the full Verification V3 operation set: descriptor/K identity and
            retained P; Runtime store isolation and passive readers; generation and
            completion fencing; transaction policy, preview and failure truth; stream
            and timer lifecycle; bounded invalidation, fanout, and trusted writes.
            - Return Contract IDs; Changed files; Focused checks; Lint pass/fail;
            Behavior reviewed; Fixed findings; Blocking findings; Remaining advisory
            findings.
            - No blocking finding or unclassified proof gap remains. Tests do not
            recreate deferred inputs or assert private implementation choreography.
